cue0090340
01:15:16.840 --> 01:15:17.700
What does it mean?

cue0090341
01:15:17.860 --> 01:15:19.100
When he does that to me, he says,

cue0090342
01:15:19.100 --> 01:15:20.880
I have enough information

cue0090343
01:15:20.880 --> 01:15:22.100
I can figure it out

cue0090344
01:15:22.100 --> 01:15:23.640
I think I have the answer

cue0090345
01:15:23.640 --> 01:15:25.120
what it means is

cue0090346
01:15:25.120 --> 01:15:27.900
we have free choice

cue0090347
01:15:27.900 --> 01:15:30.240
God is regretful

cue0090348
01:15:30.240 --> 01:15:31.840
and that's not

cue0090349
01:15:31.840 --> 01:15:33.460
a positive attribute

cue0090350
01:15:33.460 --> 01:15:35.480
but a human language

cue0090351
01:15:35.480 --> 01:15:36.720
version of how

cue0090352
01:15:36.720 --> 01:15:38.300
we would imagine

cue0090353
01:15:38.300 --> 01:15:39.560
what we're going to talk about

cue0090354
01:15:39.560 --> 01:15:41.940
we didn't live up to

cue0090355
01:15:41.940 --> 01:15:42.900
God's expectations

cue0090356
01:15:42.900 --> 01:15:45.680
God gave us free choice

cue0090357
01:15:45.680 --> 01:15:47.040
we didn't use it

cue0090358
01:15:47.040 --> 01:15:49.800
that lack of coming up to snows,

cue0090359
01:15:50.160 --> 01:15:50.880
Zinah Ḥayyim.

cue0090360
01:15:52.480 --> 01:15:55.200
Now, although the true essence of God

cue0090361
01:15:55.200 --> 01:15:56.980
cannot be known to man,

cue0090362
01:15:57.460 --> 01:15:57.840
why?

cue0090363
01:15:58.540 --> 01:16:01.600
Particularly on account of his somatic condition.

cue0090364
01:16:02.000 --> 01:16:03.440
This requires explanation.

cue0090365
01:16:04.380 --> 01:16:06.300
Somatic means body.

cue0090366
01:16:07.200 --> 01:16:08.160
Your body.

cue0090367
01:16:08.940 --> 01:16:11.580
We are limited by our body.

cue0090368
01:16:12.040 --> 01:16:13.340
As long as we're in this body,

cue0090369
01:16:14.100 --> 01:16:16.940
there's certain elements of reality

cue0090370
01:16:16.940 --> 01:16:26.140
that we cannot know because our body precedes us. My hairline recedes. My sugar count is higher than

cue0090371
01:16:26.140 --> 01:16:32.300
mine. My long-term sugar count is higher than it should be. My bad cholesterol is too high.

cue0090372
01:16:32.860 --> 01:16:39.260
My good cholesterol is too low. This impinge I see also good or good foods that for me I don't know

cue0090373
01:16:39.260 --> 01:16:45.100
why it will make me sick to eat. My body tells me I can't do certain things. I can't run like I used

cue0090374
01:16:45.100 --> 01:16:47.360
that we get over.

cue0090375
01:16:48.040 --> 01:16:49.420
This is Daraq Ko Ha'ar.

cue0090376
01:16:50.720 --> 01:16:52.400
We have a somatic condition

cue0090377
01:16:52.400 --> 01:16:53.740
that limits us.

cue0090378
01:16:54.620 --> 01:16:57.000
When Boreʾ Avlam was talking to Moshe Rabbenu,

cue0090379
01:16:57.780 --> 01:16:59.440
and Moshe Rabbenu said,

cue0090380
01:16:59.540 --> 01:17:00.580
Harina Kevod Deha,

cue0090381
01:17:00.960 --> 01:17:03.720
let me see your presence.

cue0090382
01:17:05.020 --> 01:17:06.300
What is Boreʾ Avlam saying?

cue0090383
01:17:06.960 --> 01:17:09.500
Your somatic condition.

cue0090384
01:17:10.040 --> 01:17:11.860
The fact that you are part of a body

cue0090385
01:17:11.860 --> 01:17:14.100
keeps you from doing that.

cue0090386
01:17:14.100 --> 01:17:17.100
Because what does Boreʾ ʿOlam say to Moshe Rabbenu?

cue0090387
01:17:17.100 --> 01:17:19.040
Why you can't see more of me?

cue0090388
01:17:19.040 --> 01:17:23.860
As great a Nabi as you are, you now, Mr. Moshe, are in a body.

cue0090389
01:17:23.860 --> 01:17:28.840
B'lo yirani ʾAdam lachai.

cue0090390
01:17:28.840 --> 01:17:33.480
You cannot see me and live.

cue0090391
01:17:33.480 --> 01:17:36.020
You cannot be in your so-manic condition.

cue0090392
01:17:36.020 --> 01:17:41.220
You can't be in a body with the limits that it will make upon you and live.

cue0090393
01:17:41.220 --> 01:17:43.600
What is Boreʾ ʿOlam doing here?

cue0090394
01:17:43.600 --> 01:17:46.600
We were made as animals.

cue0090395
01:17:46.600 --> 01:17:51.600
Motar ha'adam min abdehim ma'ayin

cue0090396
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:54.600
We were made animals.

cue0090397
01:17:54.600 --> 01:17:56.600
We have choice to be better.

cue0090398
01:17:56.600 --> 01:17:59.600
Boreʾ ʿOlam creates the world.

cue0090399
01:17:59.600 --> 01:18:02.600
We are given the Tora as a map and as a code

cue0090400
01:18:02.600 --> 01:18:04.600
whereby we create ourselves.

cue0090401
01:18:04.600 --> 01:18:06.600
It doesn't sound.

cue0090402
01:18:06.600 --> 01:18:09.600
But what we strive to develop as a hudh

cue0090403
01:18:09.600 --> 01:18:11.600
in the personal perfection

cue0090404
01:18:11.600 --> 01:18:12.540
deserve ʿOlam Haba.

cue0090405
01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:15.460
And if we don't make it,

cue0090406
01:18:15.720 --> 01:18:17.100
we get Tachiyat HaMeitim.

cue0090407
01:18:17.880 --> 01:18:19.100
We get Tachiyat HaMeitim,

cue0090408
01:18:19.540 --> 01:18:20.580
which is a second chance,

cue0090409
01:18:20.700 --> 01:18:22.900
